/.clwb/

# Generated visualization artifacts: graph / class-diagram renders and RDR rule
# trees written into the working tree by visualize(), render_tree() and
# render_evaluated_rule_tree() during tests and doc builds. None are committed.
pdf_graph.pdf
query_graph.pdf
class_diagram.pdf
*_explanation.pdf
*_read_tree.dot
*_read_tree.svg
*_evaluated_tree.dot
*_evaluated_tree.svg
*_rdr.dot
*_rdr.svg

# Personal, per-user Claude Code memory. Never committed on any branch.
CLAUDE.local.md

# Personal, per-user Claude Code settings. Never committed on any branch - shared
# project settings live in a committed .claude/settings.json instead.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ORMatic generates every package's ormatic_interface.py from its dataclasses, so the
# repository builds them (scripts/regenerate_all_orm.py) instead of tracking them.
# Tracking a generated file made every branch switch fail while a checkout held its own
# copy, which is what git refuses to overwrite.
**/ormatic_interface.py
# The Warsaw pipeline's scenes and its output. A run writes a directory of its own beside
# the scene it read, and none of it belongs in the repository: the scans are hundreds of
# megabytes and a run's conclusions are a run's, not the project's.
experiments/src/experiments/warsaw/dataset/
experiments/src/experiments/warsaw/pipeline_runs/
experiments/src/experiments/warsaw/evaluation/comparisons/
# The self-collision matrix a collision test saves. It is written into whatever directory
# the tests were started from, so it lands at the root of a checkout and gets swept into a
# commit; the matrices the project keeps live in
# semantic_digital_twin/resources/collision_configs/ under the robot's own name.
test.srdf

# The ground-truth mesh picked over to choose landmarks, rebuilt from the URDF export.
experiments/src/experiments/warsaw/evaluation/landmarks/*.ply

# Local data produced by the Python coverage checks.
/.coverage
/.coverage.*

# Some robokudo annotators have default models downloaded
robokudo/src/robokudo/models/
